            "Init": "1776073440940",
            "InitSubtitle": "1773728841583",
            "ErrorHandler": "1773737494589"
          },
          "code": "DECIDE_FLOW",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1769666587887",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769666587889_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_SWITCH.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Use a single multiRecordWidget generated from the input array: {{$context.$nodes.GET_REASONS.$output.result}}\n\nDo NOT generate any titles, headings, descriptive text, or summary.\nDo NOT include any text outside the multiRecordWidget.\n\n- showOnExpand for any column is false.\n\nUse these columns in EXACT order:\n\n\"Point Of Use\" (subinventory or subinventory:locator if locator exists)\n\"Expected # of Cards\" (NumberOfCards)\n\"Total\" (TotalKanbanCards)\n\"Full\" (FullCards)\n\"Empty\" (EmptyCards)\n\"New\" (NewCards)\n\"In Process\" (InprocessCards)\n\"Temporary\" (TemporaryCards)\n\"Reason\" (Badge)\n\nRules:\n- Use ONLY the data in the input array.\n- Do NOT infer, assume, normalize, or fabricate any value.\n- If a field is missing, null, or undefined, show an empty string.\n- EVERY record must have a Badge.\n- Do NOT use any existing Reason value from the input.\n- Do NOT reorder, rename, or modify any column value.\n\nNumeric conversion:\n- pctDiffTotal = parseFloat(PctDiffTotal)\n- pctDiffFull = parseFloat(PctDiffFull)\n- threshold = parseFloat($context.$variables.threshold)\n- If any parseFloat result is NaN, null, or undefined, use 0.\n- Preserve the sign exactly as provided.\n\nBadge display rules: \n- use Reason as BadgeText\n- if Reason = \"Total # of cards outside safety range\" then badge colour = red\n- if Reason = \"Full cards outside safety range\" then badge colour = yellow\n- if Reason = \"All cards within safety range\" then badge colour = green\n\nHard rules:\n- Use only these three Badge values.\n- Never output \"All cards within safety range\" when rule 1 or rule 2 is true.\n- Never invent any other Badge text.\n\nRow action for each row:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Replenish new kanban cards\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(replenishKanbanCards, replenishKanbanCards-<pullSequenceId>)\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Replenish new kanban cards\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Replenish new kanban cards\",\n  \"prioritize\": false\n}\n- Replace <pullSequenceId> with the pullSequenceId of that row."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Format Final Answer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_FINAL_ANSWER",
          "id": "1769667420378",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769667420380_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use the input :  \n      - {{$context.$nodes.GET_REASONS.$output.result}}\n      - {{$context.$nodes.FILTER_KANBAN_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES.$output.result}}\n\n- Generate row action for each row:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Replenish new kanban cards\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(replenishKanbanCards, replenishKanbanCards-<pullSequenceId>)\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Replenish new kanban cards\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Replenish new kanban cards\",\n  \"prioritize\": false\n}\n- Replace <pullSequenceId> with the pullSequenceId of that row from {{$context.$nodes.FILTER_KANBAN_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES.$output.result}}.\n- showOnExpand for any column is false."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Answering Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_ANSWERING_AGENT",
          "id": "1769668238342",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769668238344_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a context-grounded question answering agent.\n\nYou are provided with:\n1. `itemDetails` – an array containing pull-sequence-level Kanban card data for a single item: {{$context.$nodes.FILTER_KANBAN_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES.$output.result }}\n2. `chatHistory` – prior user and assistant messages in this conversation: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n3. `userQuery` – the latest user question: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nYour task:\n- Answer the `userQuery` using ONLY the information present in `itemDetails` and `chatHistory`.\n- Explain findings in clear, human-readable business language.\n\nBusiness logic (strict):\n- Having MORE cards than expected is NOT a problem and should NOT be treated as bad.\n- A pull sequence is considered BAD only if:\n  - The total number of cards is BELOW the acceptable range\n  - OR the number of available full cards is BELOW the acceptable range\n- Excess cards or cards above the upper limit should be described as healthy or safe.\n\nExplanation rules (strict):\n- Do NOT expose raw field names (e.g., internal status names or thresholds).\n- Do NOT output JSON, key-value pairs, or bullet lists of raw data fields.\n- Translate data into plain-language statements a business user would understand.\n- You MAY reference concepts like:\n  \"expected cards\", \"actual cards\", \"available full cards\",\n  \"sufficient stock\", \"shortage risk\", or \"buffer availability\".\n\nOut-of-context handling:\n- If the question cannot be answered using the given data, respond with:\n  \"I don’t have enough information in the current context to answer that.\"\n\nResponse rules:\n- Do NOT fabricate, infer, or assume information.\n- Do NOT introduce external knowledge.\n- Do NOT reference internal IDs.\n- Keep the response concise (2–4 sentences preferred).\n- Do NOT explain your reasoning steps."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Organization Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773729299011"
          },
          "code": "SET_ORGANIZATION_DETAILS",
          "id": "1769679060366",
          "inputs": [
