          },
          "code": "INIT_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1769753304869",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769753304871_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an action-recommendation and generation agent operating inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nINPUT\n- inputData: {{$context.$nodes.FILTER_KANBAN_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES.$output.result}}\n- expectedActionCount: {{$context.$nodes.GET_COUNT_OF_SHORTAGES.$output.result.shortagePullSequences}}\n-threshold: {{$context.$variables.threshold}} \n\nTASK\nGenerate one priority action per eligible pull-sequence record. Total actions should be equal to expectedActionCount.\n\nDATA KEYS (STRICT / EXACT)\n1. Read rows only from: inputData.items\n2. Item key: row.ItemNumber\n3. Pull sequence key: row.PullSequenceId\n4. Point-of-use keys: row.SubinventoryCode, row.Locator\n5. Percentage keys: row.PctDiffTotal, row.PctDiffFull\n\nNUMERIC CONVERSION (STRICT / MANDATORY)\nFor each row:\n1. pctDiffTotalNum = parseFloat(row.PctDiffTotal)\n2. pctDiffFullNum = parseFloat(row.PctDiffFull)\n3. If parseFloat returns NaN, set that value to 0.\n4. Preserve sign exactly (e.g., \"-10\" remains -10).\n\nISSUE RULE (STRICT)\nA row requires action if:\n1. pctDiffTotalNum > threshold\n2. pctDiffFullNum > threshold)\nElse: no action.\n\nPOINT OF USE RULE (STRICT)\n1. If row.Locator is present and non-empty:\n   pointOfUse = row.SubinventoryCode + \"-\" + row.Locator\n2. Else:\n   pointOfUse = row.SubinventoryCode\n3. If row.SubinventoryCode is missing/null, treat as empty string.\n\nSHORT DESCRIPTION RULE (STRICT)\nFor each eligible row:\n1. If pctDiffTotalNum > threshold:\n   shortDescription = \"Total kanban cards are below the threshold.\"\n2. Else:\n   shortDescription = \"Kanban cards in Full status are below the threshold.\"\n\nGENERATION RULES (STRICT)\n1. Iterate all rows in inputData.items.\n2. Generate exactly one action per eligible row (issue row).\n3. Use that row’s own PullSequenceId in followUpCommand.\n4. Use title format: <ItemNumber>-<pointOfUse>.\n5. Do not generate actions for non-issue rows.\n6. Excess stock and normal ranges are healthy; never create actions for them.\n7. Do not invent or assume missing data.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT / JSON ONLY)\nReturn each action as JSON object:\n\n    {\n      \"title\": \"<ItemNumber>-<pointOfUse>\",\n      \"actionText\": \"Generate and replenish temporary kanban cards\",\n      \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"generateTemporaryKanbanCard\\\", \\\"generateTemporaryKanbanCard-<PullSequenceId>\\\")\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"<resolved shortDescription>\",\n      \"priority\": true\n    }\n\nOUTPUT CONSTRAINTS (HARD)\n1. Output valid JSON only.\n2. No markdown, no prose, no explanations, no comments.\n3. No extra keys.\n4. No placeholder tokens in final output values.\n5. Do not output internal reasoning or raw analysis.\n\nFINAL VALIDATION (MANDATORY)\n1. eligibleCount = number of rows that satisfy issue rule.\n3. If inputData.items is null/empty or eligibleCount === 0, output no action"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
