          "code": "RETURN_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1769765956297",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769765956300_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are responsible for informing the user whether the replenishment action was successful or not.\n\nYou have the following context:\n1. {{$context.$nodes.REPLENISH_ALL_KANBAN_CARDS.$output}} — the response of the API call which replenishes the kanban cards.\n2. {{$context.$nodes.REPLENISH_ALL_KANBAN_CARDS.$status}} — the status of the API call.\n3. {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_KANBAN_CARDS_FOR_PULLSEQUENCE_ID.$output}} — get any info like ItemNumber, etc.\n4. {{$context.$nodes.GET_LIST_OF_KANBAN_CARDS.$output.result}} — the array of Kanban cards available for replenishment.\n\nInstructions:\n- If {{$context.$nodes.GET_LIST_OF_KANBAN_CARDS.$output.result}} is null or an empty array, output:  \n  “No kanban cards found in new or full status to replenish. Consider generating a temporary kanban card.”\n- Otherwise, if replenishment or adjustment is performed successfully with REPLENISH_ALL_KANBAN_CARDS:\n    - Output a plain, friendly sentence summarizing:\n        - The list of Kanban cards (by number) that were replenished or adjusted.\n        - The relevant action taken for each card (e.g., replenished, reclaimed, inactivated, adjusted from FULL).\n        - The ItemNumber from {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_KANBAN_CARDS_FOR_PULLSEQUENCE_ID.$output}} (mention only once if all cards have the same ItemNumber).\n        - The specific point of failure or issue addressed (e.g., \"card count above range\", \"full cards below range\").\n    - No extra explanation, technical details, or formatting—just the single summary sentence.\n- If no Kanban cards needed replenishment or adjustment:\n    - Output the following sentence: “No Kanban cards required replenishment or adjustment for this pullSequenceId.”\n- If the REPLENISH_ALL_KANBAN_CARDS call encounters an error:\n    - Output a brief error summary sentence indicating the failure and suggest a retry or escalation."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
